From 81ea7372ba0ed7141873d4040b861a4897d2fb37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:32:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SimAntics: approach positions, object selection, free will,
 queue recovery, conversations

Roadmap items 2, 4, 5, 6 and 10 (partial). Each is behind its own
VMFeatures switch (default on) so it can be compared with the original
behaviour from Simitone's settings dialog.

ApproachPositions (2):
- VMSlotParser no longer offers a seat another avatar sits in (slot 0
  holds the sitter); the route fails with DestChairOccupied and the
  sitter as blocker, instead of walking there and failing with CantSit.
- When a goal fails, the remaining slot positions are checked against
  the lot as it is now: dropped if an object or a sitter took them,
  tried last if a Sim stands there or is heading there. Positions are
  only filtered and reordered, never invented.
- Diagnostics: a Choices route event lists why positions were left out.

ObjectSelection (4): find best object for function prefers objects in
rooms reachable through doors and stairs (VMReachability) that the
caller has not failed to route to in the last Sim hour
(VMRouteFailMemory, recorded at route hard-fail, transient). With no
such object the original answer is returned unchanged.

AutonomyFixes (6): free will skips objects with a running lockout count
(set by the Standard Exit tree, 20-500 ticks for most objects), and
scores unreachable objects x0.01 and recently failed ones x0.1.
AutonomyCountOnce (6, balance): an action with several pie entries was
added once per entry as its first entry; it now counts once.

QueueRecovery (5): when the running action's object is deleted, the Sim
is reset as before but its other queued actions are put back; only the
deleted object's action and its sub-actions are dropped (Pruned).
OnActionEnded now fires whether or not diagnostics are recorded and
carries the action UID, for the client's queue notices.

Conversations (10, partial): a free-will route waits for socialising
Sims instead of shooing them (player commands still shoo); a route to a
Sim who moved more than 1.5 tiles re-targets them, up to 3 times.

Tests: reachability flood and failure memory (Simitone routing tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
